>
  <p>Consistency in sizing is the #1 factor for customer retention in the activewear industry. For sourcing managers, understanding how to communicate technical measurements to a factory is essential to avoid costly sampling errors.</p>
  
  <div class="my-10 max-w-[500px] mx-auto">
    <img src="https://sc01.alicdn.com/kf/Hd0c3263605304eb597b07fc2786e7361E.jpg" alt="Leggings Measurement Guide" class="w-full rounded-2xl shadow-xl" />
  </div>

  <h2>Key Measurement Points</h2>
  <p>When providing a tech pack for yoga leggings, focus on these four critical points:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Waist:</strong> Measured flat across the top of the waistband. For high-waist styles, the tension of the internal elastic is as important as the measurement.</li>
    <li><strong>Hip:</strong> Usually measured 15-20cm below the waistband. This determines the overall silhouette and compression level.</li>
    <li><strong>Inseam:</strong> Measured from the crotch gusset to the bottom hem. This defines if the style is "7/8 length" or "Full length."</li>
    <li><strong>Full Length:</strong> The total vertical distance from the top edge to the leg opening.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Importance of Tolerance</h2>
  <p>Due to the high elasticity of Nylon/Spandex blends, we maintain a strict <strong>+/- 1cm tolerance</strong>. Our pattern-making team uses these precise metrics to ensure that your "Small" in China fits exactly like a "Small" in the US or Europe.</p>
